ravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm","html_url":"https://github.com/bnjmntmm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-16T14:28:01Z","updated_at":"2025-07-16T14:28:01Z","body":"What does the one failed Linux / Editor with Mono mean? \r\nWill squash later in the evening","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3078858350/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3079056522","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108644#issuecomment-3079056522","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108644","id":3079056522,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63hqyK","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-16T15:06:26Z","updated_at":"2025-07-16T15:06:26Z","body":"> What does the one failed Linux / Editor with Mono mean?\r\n\r\nIt wants you to change the order if the property in the XML docs - I think it alphabetizes them?\r\n\r\nHere's the patch it gives:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/modules/openxr/doc_classes/OpenXRCompositionLayer.xml b/modules/openxr/doc_classes/OpenXRCompositionLayer.xml\r\nindex 38ade44..8921f8e 100644\r\n--- a/modules/openxr/doc_classes/OpenXRCompositionLayer.xml\r\n+++ b/modules/openxr/doc_classes/OpenXRCompositionLayer.xml\r\n@@ -49,6 +49,10 @@\r\n \t\t<member name=\"layer_viewport\" type=\"SubViewport\" setter=\"set_layer_viewport\" getter=\"get_layer_viewport\">\r\n \t\t\tThe [SubViewport] to render on the composition layer.\r\n \t\t</member>\r\n+\t\t<member name=\"protected_content\" type=\"bool\" setter=\"set_protected_content\" getter=\"is_protected_content\" default=\"false\">\r\n+\t\t\tIf enabled, the OpenXR swapchain will be created with the [code]XR_SWAPCHAIN_CREATE_PROTECTED_CONTENT_BIT[/code] flag, which will protect its contents from CPU access.\r\n+\t\t\tWhen used with an Android Surface, this may allow DRM content to be presented, and will only take effect when the Surface is first created; later changes to this property will have no effect.\r\n+\t\t</member>\r\n \t\t<member name=\"sort_order\" type=\"int\" setter=\"set_sort_order\" getter=\"get_sort_order\" default=\"1\">\r\n \t\t\tThe sort order for this composition layer. Higher numbers will be shown in front of lower numbers.\r\n \t\t\t[b]Note:[/b] This will have no effect if a fallback mesh is being used.\r\n@@ -102,10 +106,6 @@\r\n \t\t\tSee [method get_android_surface] for information about how to get the surface so that your application can draw to it.\r\n \t\t\t[b]Note:[/b] This will only work in Android builds.\r\n \t\t</member>\r\n-\t\t<member name=\"protected_content\" type=\"bool\" setter=\"set_protected_content\" getter=\"is_protected_content\" default=\"false\">\r\n-\t\t\tIf enabled, the OpenXR swapchain will be created with the [code]XR_SWAPCHAIN_CREATE_PROTECTED_CONTENT_BIT[/code] flag, which will protect its contents from CPU access.\r\n-\t\t\tWhen used with an Android Surface, this may allow DRM content to be presented, and will only take effect when the Surface is first created; later changes to this property will have no effect.\r\n-\t\t</member>\r\n \t</members>\r\n \t<constants>\r\n \t\t<constant name=\"FILTER_NEAREST\" value=\"0\" enum=\"Filter\">\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo, just moving that section up to be below `layer_viewport`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3079056522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3079229407","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108644#issuecomment-3079229407","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108644","id":3079229407,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63iU_f","user":{"login":"bnjmntmm","id":8472232,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0NzIyMzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8472232?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm","html_url":"https://github.com/bnjmntmm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bnjmntmm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.co